  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Contributed Funds</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This cooperative agreement will convene technology developers and field practitioners for the first time, to identify high tech tools that are available and could be adapted or customized for rhino conservation activities in order to ensure that all African range states and rhino custodians have access to the best technology available to protect wild rhinos. Specific activities will include convening approximately 40 key representatives of field programs and military, police, and customs authorities from all eight African rhino range states in Namibia in November 2012. Technology developers, including the manufacturers of RFID tags, transmitters, unmanned aerial vehicles, and remote sensing equipment will also be invited to present their equipment and to help identify new features that could facilitate rhino protection.</narrative>
  </description>
